---
source: crates/odx-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: cmd.render_long_help().to_string()
---
Take one entry's action

Usage: odx dashboard act [OPTIONS] <--include|--port|--mute|--drop|--follow|--promote> <ID>

Arguments:
  <ID>
          The entry id, as the dashboard shows it

Options:
      --include
          Add the pull request to the project

      --port
          Port the change: cherry-picked onto a branch of the target series in a clone under the cache

      --open-pr
          With --port: then push the branch and open a draft pull request; with --promote: write the promotion and open its pull request

      --mute
          Record a mute (or, with an organisation kind, a verdict)

      --drop
          Remove the override from the project

      --follow
          Take the index update

      --promote
          Promote the addon into the next environment (the plan; --open-pr writes it)

      --reason <REASON>
          Why (mandatory with --mute)

      --kind <KIND>
          Kind of the mute or verdict

          Possible values:
          - not-applicable:  The change does not apply to the target series
          - not-needed:      The change is not needed on the target series
          - superseded:      Superseded by another change
          - already-present: Already present on the target, possibly by another route
          - declined:        Declined for this project
          - not-wanted:      Not wanted in this project
          - deferred:        Review later; re-checked on expiry and on target code changes
          
          [default: not-wanted]

      --until <DATE>
          With --mute: when it expires (YYYY-MM-DD)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Global options:
  -C, --project-dir <DIR>
          Run as if started in DIR

  -c, --config <FILE>
          The pyproject.toml to use (a repos.yaml for the commands that read one)

  -j, --jobs <N>
          Override the number of parallel jobs

      --offline
          Serve git repositories and forge and index data from the cache only; what is not cached fails. Local work (git, pre-commit, odoo-lint) takes as long as before

      --fresh
          Ignore cached data; refresh everything before answering

      --no-refresh
          Use cached data even when stale. Like --offline, this saves network time only

      --refresh-index
          Rebuild the addon index for the series involved

      --json
          Machine-readable output on stdout

  -v, --verbose...
          Say when each repository's fetch and build starts, and what each fetched and merged

  -q, --quiet
          Errors only on standard error: no progress lines, no warnings
